A new dashboard service gives access to more than 20 AI models including chat GPT, Claude and Gemini inside a single interface for a flat monthly fee of $79.

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:50.240
You can switch between models instantly and compare how each one answers the same question without opening multiple tabs or apps.

00:05:50.840 --> 00:05:57.060
This is helpful when you want to see different writing styles or pick the answer that feels clearest for a homework question.

00:05:57.060 --> 00:06:07.120
Once you have access, type the same simple question into two different models side by side and notice how their sentence structure and level of detail change.

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:15.940
Think of it like having a row of different tutors in one room and being able to ask each the exact same question without walking between classrooms.

00:06:15.940 --> 00:06:29.000
A Munich court ruled that the AI music tool Suno violated copyright by both storing six specific songs inside its model during training and reproducing parts of them in new outputs.

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:41.380
The court rejected Germany's text and data mining exception as well as the US fair use defense showing that legal questions about AI training data are still being decided case by case.

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:52.060
High school students are increasingly turning to AI chat bots for help choosing classes, writing applications and planning college visits instead of speaking with human counselors.

00:06:52.900 --> 00:07:01.920
The trend raises practical questions about how much personal guidance should come from a program versus a trained advisor who knows the students full situation.

